PATCH 622: preserve active-channel SHR/ADD bytes and DS-relative mixer storage (board:0003).

Original 2630 reads each channel byte, shifts AL/DL by the self-modified immediate
at 2689/26b3/26df, adds the byte at 268b/26b6/26e2, then accumulates AX. Shift
counts use the original x86 low-five-bit contract; the widened byte shift is
zero for effective counts 8..31, and the result/addition wraps to eight bits.
The old C skips all six operations. At the reached IRQ before KDV callback 168,
original operands are SHR 1/2/3 and ADD 40/60/70 hex.

26fe/270b read/write the feedback byte at DS:(1621+(1619 & 161d)); the previous
host address 1621 loses DS. 2714 reads a BYTE at EAX plus the mutable displacement
stored at 2716. Use the shared flat-operand resolver for either an original
module offset or the port's existing host-pointer representation. Never apply
Ghidra's four-byte DAT_2093 indexing or hard-code the selected lookup table.

The paired paging-aware original snapshot and complete trace prove this active
1024-output block without channel rollover. Samples are read from provisioned
DSOUNDS.BIN by hash/offset; no game sample assets are added to Git. The regression
checks the full one-MiB module state, every mixed byte and the untouched DMA half.
Channel rollover/register callbacks, IRQ/device setup and elapsed mixer work
remain open. This patch does not replace any of them with an aggregate delay.
